1. She was a student in the past and experienced financial hardship, often being hungry. (Verbatim: "I was a student at the time, so I was also hungry.")
2. She once participated in a Godiva chocolate taste-testing event that initially seemed suspicious, as she was approached by a stranger on a dark winter night. (Verbatim: "I was walking along the streets. It was dark. It was winter. It was cold and raining... And then I come across as a person. Hello. Hi, stranger. Do you want some chocolate?")
3. She has never had cavities or needed braces, and she considers her dental health to be very fortunate. (Verbatim: "I've never had any like issues, cavities. I've never had to need like any sort of braces or anything like that.")
4. She has sensitive teeth and uses sensitive toothpaste. (Verbatim: "The only thing I do have is sensitive teeth. So I have to have like the sensitive like, you know, toothpaste and stuff.")
5. As a child, she was extremely obsessed with sugar and would eat it directly from the box, including icing sugar and golden syrup. (Verbatim: "As a kid, I used to eat just sugar from the box... I used to grab the icing sugar, a spoon, and a little glass of water. Yeah, and then I used to just drink the golden syrup.")
6. She would climb the fridge like "a heckin' spider" to reach hidden sugar as a child. (Verbatim: "I used to climb the fridge to try and get to it, like a heckin' spider, like Spider-Man, just climb up to get on top of the fridge to get the sugar that they were hiding from me.")
7. She skipped taking the bus to school in order to save money to buy chocolate. (Verbatim: "I used to skip getting the bus and walk to school so I could save on the bus money so that I could buy chocolate.")
8. She has a nostalgic connection to cheap chocolate from advent calendars and recognizes its distinct waxy taste. (Verbatim: "This tastes exactly like calendar chocolate... The wax taste is from the wax molding?")
9. She associates pink-colored items with Valentine's Day, even if not explicitly themed. (Verbatim: "But anything pink apparently is Valentine's themed, so that will do.")
10. She grew up eating Tesco Value brand chocolate and initially believed it was the best chocolate, only later realizing it was cheap. (Verbatim: "My nan would always buy me the, like, Tesco Value brand chocolate. And I always thought it was, like, the best thing in the entire universe... to find out that it's actually just the cheap chocolate I was tasting.") [end of text]



1. She had no friends during a certain period of her life. (Verbatim: "I didn't have friends at that time.")
2. She walked a couple of miles to school, sometimes taking the bus for part of the journey. (Verbatim: "Did I have to walk far for school? It's quite far, yeah. Sometimes I walked and still got the bus part of the way. It was a couple of miles, I would say.")
3. She was underweight as a child but was mocked for being overweight, which confused and shocked her. (Verbatim: "I was a very underweight kid. A lot of people made fun of me for being overweight.")
4. She experienced bullying in school for being different, including being called names like "stick" due to her thin frame. (Verbatim: "I used to get called a stick or something.")
5. She was once insulted by a smaller child at a store who called her a "fat pig," which stood out because it contradicted how she was usually perceived. (Verbatim: "And this small, tiny little child... looked at me... and I was like, pig. Fat pig.")
6. She reflects that people will mock others regardless of appearance or differences, citing examples like weight, hair color, ethnicity, and being quiet. (Verbatim: "people make fun of you no matter what... too much weight they're gonna make fun of you, too little weight they're gonna make fun of you...")
7. She is glad she did not accept a scholarship to attend a private school, as students there were bullied for being poor. (Verbatim: "I am glad I didn't take the scholarship though and go to private school because apparently the kids that did really did get made fun of for being poor.")
8. She has a nostalgic connection to cheap chocolate, associating it with her childhood despite its poor quality. (Verbatim: "it tastes like my childhood.")
9. She dislikes raspberry ripple ice cream and used to eat around the ripples, leaving only the ripple parts behind. (Verbatim: "i don't like raspberry ripple... i used to eat raspberry ripple by eating around the ripples and just leaving the ripples in the tub.")
10. She used to eat only one flavor at a time from Neapolitan ice cream, rejecting the idea of mixing them. (Verbatim: "i was the kid that just ate one flavor and ruined it... it was just three ice creams in one but you know what i just felt like one.") [end of text]



1. She was the middle child and felt like the "forgotten child" who was not the favorite. (Verbatim: "as you guys know based on my behavior i was the middle child the forgotten child the definitely not favorite child so they never took my side")

2. She had two brothers and often clashed with them, especially over food. (Verbatim: "my brother would go up to my mother and be like ew elliot just ate the vanilla part of the raspberry ripple and i'd be like you absolute snitch")

3. As a child, she was well-behaved in terms of manners and being quiet, but sneaky about food. (Verbatim: "i was as good a child as could be in terms of like manners um being quiet etc but when it came to food i was a sneak i was a big sneak when it came to food")

4. She once ate an entire batch of cupcakes by climbing onto the kitchen counter to reach them. (Verbatim: "i climbed the counters and grabbed it... and another and another and until they were all gone")

5. She did not understand the concept of being "grounded" as a punishment because she preferred staying home. (Verbatim: "you're grounded and i'd be like what the heck is this grounded thing... i think it's a reward")

6. Her parents told her she wasn’t allowed to go outside because she might get kidnapped, unlike her brothers. (Verbatim: "they would be like oh any you can't go out you'll get kidnapped")

7. Her parents jokingly claimed her brothers were allowed outside because they were ugly and thus not worth kidnapping. (Verbatim: "that's because your brothers are ugly so no one would want to kidnap them")

8. She was bullied as a child for being ugly, contradicting her parents' joke about her looks. (Verbatim: "if i was i wouldn't have got bullied for being ugly")

9. She has a nostalgic connection to Freddo chocolate bars and remembers them being available for a long time. (Verbatim: "this is a freddo freddo is i assume the name of the frog... i'm surprised is still available")

10. She expresses confusion about historical currency like shillings, indicating limited knowledge of pre-decimal British money. (Verbatim: "i don't even know what shilling was") [end of text]



